# /security-auditor — App + Supabase security audit

This rule triggers the **security-auditor** skill. Read `.claude/skills/security-auditor/SKILL.md` and follow it strictly.

## What this does

- Takes a **mode**: `full` (default), `db`, `app`, `dashboard`, or `delta`
- Audits against SPEC 12, SPEC 13, `references/security/checklist.md`, and the skill checklists
- Optionally checks Supabase security advisors via MCP when available
- **Report only by default** — no code, migration, or dashboard changes unless the human explicitly requests fixes
- Updates memory in `references/security/audit-log.md`

## What this does NOT do

- Implement fixes or write migrations by default
- Mark specs as `Aprobado` or write new specs (recommend `@spec` for new scope)
- Replace pentest or compliance certification
- Audit game canvas mechanics unless tied to scores/auth

## Supporting files

- `.claude/skills/security-auditor/SKILL.md` — six-phase workflow and hard rules
- `.claude/skills/security-auditor/app-security-checklist.md` — Next.js, proxy, auth, actions, APIs
- `.claude/skills/security-auditor/db-security-checklist.md` — RLS, functions, migrations, advisors
- `specs/12-auth-supabase.md` — auth and profiles model
- `specs/13-security-hardening.md` — hardening baseline
- `references/security/checklist.md` — operational checklist
- `references/security/audit-log.md` — audit inventory (read at start, update at end)
- `references/supabase-auth-setup.md` — dashboard Auth and advisor steps

## Workflow summary

1. **Context** — read specs, checklist, audit-log, checklists, sensitive code paths
2. **Confirm mode** — from argument or default `full`
3. **Audit repo** — walk checklists read-only (or delta on git diff)
4. **Advisors** — Supabase MCP if available; else manual follow-up
5. **Report** — findings table + checklist summary
6. **Persist** — update snapshot + append session in `audit-log.md`, then **STOP**

## Subagent

For a clean context, delegate to [`.cursor/agents/security-auditor.md`](.cursor/agents/security-auditor.md) when the user explicitly asks for the `@security-auditor` subagent.

## Example invocations

```
@security-auditor
@security-auditor full
@security-auditor db
@security-auditor app
@security-auditor dashboard
@security-auditor delta
```

## When to invoke

- After auth, Supabase, or API changes
- Before production deploy
- Periodic regression (`full`)
- After Auth dashboard changes (`dashboard`)

## Handoff

| Finding type | Next step |
|--------------|-----------|
| New capability (CSP, rate limit, 2FA) | `@spec` |
| Approved spec | `@spec-impl` |
| Explicit fix request | Implement in same thread when user asks |
| Generic PR review | `/review-security` (complement, not replacement) |
